  "name": "Future funk (vaporwave subgenre)",
  "family": "electronic",
  "lineage": "Mid-2010s vaporwave-derived electronic subgenre integrating French house, disco, and Japanese city-pop sampling into accessible, uplifting dance-music. Saint Pepsi (later Skylar Spence), Yung Bae, Macross 82-99, and the broader Business Casual and Local Business label rosters anchor the canonical future funk aesthetic. Distinguished from broader vaporwave by future funk's explicit dance-functional and uplifting (vs vaporwave's ironic-melancholic) emotional register.",
  "recipe": "classic 2014-2016 future funk, groove Percussion, funk percussive branch, east Asian pop functional song, ambient experimental electric enka k-indie. thick, breath veiled tone, slow rate, interlocked note trading. TR-808, fast decay focused low lead analog synth, mahogany ernie ball slinky electric bass. no single room 2015-present distributed distributed production. FET condenser, transformerless solid-state pre, brick-wall limiter, parametric EQ. 16-bit digital.",
